# document_claims.p0t — SC2-A: frase, claim e commitment restano separati.
#
# Fonti vere e parafrasi corte:
# - Salmonella simulation study:
#   https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/
# - NASA DART technical report:
#   https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804
#
# Le tre formule epistemiche entrano parlando come membri di classi naturali.
# Il C non contiene quelle formule e il retract deve cambiare anche claim gia'
# osservate senza cancellare superficie, fonte o attribuzione.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test long units survive and multiword markers are teachable]
!timeout 60
# Il primo periodo supera la profondita' che SC1 materializzava: deve restare
# intero anche se non possiede ancora uno status.
> read: The investigators predict that higher initial Salmonella counts increase the likelihood of septic shock and death. The model outputs show that outcomes were highly correlated with initial Salmonella counts.
< Learned 0 fact(s), skipped 2.
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_0, 0)
!query document_unit_token_surface(document_1_unit_0, 16, death)
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_1, 1)
!query! current_document_typed_claim(document_1_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)

# La menzione quotata conserva la locuzione esatta attraverso learn/query/retract.
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
> Is "the investigators predict that" a hypothesis report marker?
< Yes.
> forget that "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker
< I no longer treat «"the investigators predict that"» as a hypothesis report marker.
> Is "the investigators predict that" a hypothesis report marker?
< No.
!query! hypothesis_report_marker(forget)

[test source addressed claims status and ablation]
!timeout 60
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
> "the measurements indicate that" is an observation report marker.
< Learned: observation_report_marker("the measurements indicate that").
> "the model outputs show that" is a simulation result marker.
< Learned: simulation_result_marker("the model outputs show that").

# REPLAY: una ipotesi attribuita e un risultato simulato non diventano fatti
# del mondo. URI + fingerprint generano lo stesso document id fra processi.
> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/ The investigators predict that high infection increases mortality. The model outputs show that outcomes correlate with initial infection.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4996536/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_53e12a4bf22efa6c)
!query claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query! claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, observed)
!query claim_status(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_1_claim_0, simulated)
!query claim_attributed_to(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, document_authors)
!query claim_commitment(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query holds_in(context(document_0c04338180aa7436_53e12a4bf22efa6c_unit_0_claim_0), proposition(surface("high infection increases mortality")))

# TRANSFER sperimentale: status opposti nello stesso documento e nessuna
# promozione della frase ipotizzata a commitment del mondo.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The investigators predict that kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit. The measurements indicate that DART shortened the orbital period of Dimorphos.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_ed942df7bdb84575)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query! holds_in(world, proposition(surface("kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit")))

# TRANSFER osservazionale: il risultato riportato resta distinto dalla
# conclusione causale ipotizzata, sotto una fonte open-access diversa.
> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/ The investigators predict that observational associations can misrepresent causal effects. The measurements indicate that some observational associations differed from randomized effects.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5118066/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_be8b48c1dd3343bc)
!query claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_1_claim_0, observed)
!query! claim_status(document_5c0b5aed1874ec5b_be8b48c1dd3343bc_unit_0_claim_0, observed)

# TRANSFER di simulazione climatica: `simulated` non collassa in `observed`.
> read: https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/ The investigators predict that high resolution improves predictive skill. The model outputs show that high resolution improved precipitation forecasts.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s), 2 reported claim(s), and 2 live epistemic status(es)
!query current_document_source("https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/")
!query current_document_fingerprint(fnv1a64_cb48b8510480033c)
!query claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_1_claim_0, simulated)
!query! claim_status(document_60abb92fbf13d97b_cb48b8510480033c_unit_1_claim_0, observed)

# ABLATION: lo status e il context dipendente spariscono dal documento vecchio;
# proposition, fonte e attribuzione restano. Il risultato osservato non dipende
# dalla classe ritratta e rimane vivo.
> forget that "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker
< I no longer treat «"the investigators predict that"» as a hypothesis report marker.
!query! claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query document_claim(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575, document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, proposition(surface("kinetic impact can alter an asteroid orbit")))
!query claim_attributed_to(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, document_authors)
!query claim_source_span(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0, range(32, 42))
!query! claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_1_claim_0, observed)

# RETEACH riattiva la vista sul documento gia' osservato, senza rileggerlo.
> "the investigators predict that" is a hypothesis report marker.
< Learned: hypothesis_report_marker("the investigators predict that").
!query claim_status(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, hypothesized)
!query claim_commitment(document_0246e706600fd069_ed942df7bdb84575_unit_0_claim_0, attributed_only)
